{
    "test_name": "MOB.731_AssetLookup_Proximity_Radius",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.731_AssetLookup_Proximity_Radius",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.731` **The LOCATION half of \"Near Me\"** \u2014 the half `MOB.730` could not reach.\n- **Why it exists now**: the checklist said a runner cannot satisfy `getCurrentPosition`.\n  `MOB.974` measured that and it is **false** \u2014 the methods on `navigator.geolocation` are\n  writable, and probe **G3 proved the app consumes a stubbed position**. Third inherited\n  *\"not automatable\"* row to fall this week, after offline and the map.\n- **Proves**: the label flips `Near Me` \u2192 `Within 25 mi` (and `Near Me` is **gone**);\n  `Update my location`/`Clear` appear \u2014 `MOB.730` proves they are absent without a radius,\n  so the pair proves the `{!!value}` branch; **the radius reaches the QUERY**; and a\n  `Location updated` toast, which only fires on a resolved position.\n- \u2b50 **The query assertion is deliberately an OR**: rows showing `mi away`, *or* the empty\n  state reading `No Assets Within 25 mi`. Both prove the filter ran **with the right\n  radius**, and the OR keeps the test independent of whether a fixture asset happens to\n  sit near the stubbed coordinates \u2014 geography is not a dependency a test should carry.\n- \ud83d\uded1 **EVERY DISTANCE UNIT HERE IS MATCHED AS `(mi|km)`, DELIBERATELY.** The radius items,\n  the button label, the empty state and `formatDistance` all take their suffix from the\n  **browser locale** (`utils/distance`), not from the app. This test pinned `25 miles`\n  and had been unable to find its own radius since the 2026-09-02 localization commit \u2014\n  fixed 09-08 by the codebase-sync audit, never by a run.\n- \u2b50 **`25` is the radius on purpose**: it is the only one offered in BOTH option sets\n  (imperial `5/10/25/50/100`, metric `10/25/50/100/200`), so the click cannot become\n  locale-dependent. Do not change it to another value.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **Three measured constraints**: the stub **does not survive a navigation** (so there\n  is exactly one `go()`); every menu click is gated on a **polling assert, never a bare\n  `wait`**; and the radius **persists and auto-locates on mount**, so restore is belt\n  **and** braces \u2014 `Clear`, then remove the key, then assert it is gone.\n- \ud83d\uded1 **Not covered**: auto-locate-on-mount. It needs a navigation, after which the stub is\n  gone and the mount effect races the runner. A real limit, not an omission.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Asset Lookup",
            "Geolocation"
        ],
